description:
Logs reading for a book in the reader's ReadingRate library: pages read, the page they reached, or a note. It sets the book's current page, adds the pages to today's entry in their reading journal, and adds the note to that entry. One journal entry per book per day: a second call the same day extends that day's pages and appends the note. A book on the want-to-read list moves to reading.

Use when the user says how many pages they read, which page they are on, or wants a thought about today's reading saved with it. For a book not yet in their library, use add_book_to_library first.

Give pages_read (pages read since the last log), current_page (the arabic page reached) or roman_page (a page of an introduction or preface numbered in roman numerals), only one of them; a note can be sent alone. Each call logs again, so do not repeat a call that succeeded.

Introductions numbered i, ii, iii… count. When the reader says their copy's introduction runs to a roman page (for example lx), send front_matter_ends_on with it, alone or with the page; the copy keeps it, and later arabic pages count after it. "0" means the copy has none, or the reader skipped it, which takes its pages back out.

Examples:
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "pages_read": 30}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "current_page": 150}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "front_matter_ends_on": "lx", "roman_page": "liv"}
- {"book_id": "<book id>", "notes": "The argument only lands once you have read the footnotes."}
